  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "The table below gives the values of ${\u03a6}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=\u03a6(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.001.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${\u03a6}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 3.0902)=0.999.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 3.0902)=1-0.999=0.001.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\n\u03a6(-3.0902)=0.001.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/assets/12d4d863466f8a7c1ff72d5c08fed94097ac23d94e04a2976603a3f3a78f6261.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(-3.0902) & =0.001 \\\\ P(Z\\le -3.0902) & =0.001.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-3.0902.$",
